form; online-only automated investment advisory services through Advisor, a Web-based tool. The company also provides flexible spending accounts (FSA) for health and dependent care; health reimbursement arrangements; and Consolidated Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act continuation services, as well as administers pre-tax commuter benefit programs. In addition, the company offers HSA and FSA members with access to certain healthcare products, programs, and services through its marketplace. It serves clients through a direct sales force; and brokers and advisors, a network of health plans, benefits administrators, benefits brokers and consultants, and retirement plan record-keepers. HealthEquity, Inc. was incorporated in 2002 and is based in Draper, Utah.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Scott R. Cutler J.D. | CEO, President & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $467K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 28%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $162K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $26K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["HealthEquity, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $8.6B market cap on $1.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years and +26% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 59% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $455M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 35 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.12\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.6\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (75% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.25},{"text":"Significant goodwill (49% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 25% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 21% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Piotroski score 9/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Financial quality scores above most Healthcare peers","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"HealthEquity (HQY) Could Be 14% Undervalued As HSA Market Access Expands","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-hqy/healthequity/news/healthequity-hqy-could-be-14-undervalued-as-hsa-market-acces","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794554500.887,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.925,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (HQY) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/38/Avoiding_Lag:_Real-Time_Signals_in_HQY_Movement_111126064401_1794440641.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794440641.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"HealthEquity (HQY) Jumped, But What Is Drawing Fresh Attention Now?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-hqy/healthequity/news/healthequity-hqy-jumped-but-what-is-drawing-fresh-attention","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793868152.93,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.931,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Reasons to Add HealthEquity Stock to Your Portfolio for Now","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/reasons-add-healthequity-stock-portfolio-150500372.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793977500.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.844,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"HealthEquity Schedules Third Quarter Earnings Release Date","source":"finance.yah